    "title": "Storage, bandwidth, budget",
    "body": "**Storage:** 50 million players × about 100 bytes = **5 GB**, small enough to keep in memory. **Bandwidth:** the top-100 list is about 10 KB; at 5,000 reads per second that is 50 MB per second, easy for a cache. **Latency budget** for \"my rank\" (200 ms): about 100 ms of network, 10 ms in the load balancer and server, 5 ms in the store, 85 ms to spare. **Cost:** about 10 servers and one in-memory store with a copy, a few thousand dollars a month at assumed prices.",
