    "title": "API and data model",
    "body": "**API:** `POST /scores {score}` answers 202 Accepted; `GET /leaderboard/top?n=100`; `GET /leaderboard/me` returns rank and score. The player comes from the login (SD 13), never from the request body. **Data model:** in the database, `best_scores(player_id, score, updated_at)` with `player_id` as the key; in an in-memory store, a **sorted set** of (score, player) that keeps players ordered by score, for ranks and the top 100.",
