  {
    "title": "High-level design",
    "body": "Walk one request through the boxes. A new score goes phone → load balancer → app server, which updates `best_scores` **only if the score is higher** and, in the same transaction, writes an outbox row (SD 10); a relay copies it to the sorted set, again only if higher, so a crash loses nothing and a late lower score cannot win. \"Top 100\" is cached for 1 second in front of the servers, so 5,000 reads per second hit the cache, not the store. \"My rank\" reads the sorted set. Every box answers a requirement: if a box serves none, it is not needed.",
