  {
    "title": "Deep dive: the ranking",
    "body": "The hardest requirements are N2 and N3 at 10,000 writes per second, so the deep dive goes there. A sorted set keeps its members in score order, like a balanced search tree (Level 8), so finding a player's rank takes about **log₂(50 million) ≈ 26 steps**, not a scan of 50 million rows. Assume one store node handles 100,000 updates per second and 25 GB: 10,000 updates and 5 GB fit easily, with a replica for failover. The relay copies each new best within about a second, so it shows well within 5 seconds.",
